# Ink & Garden — Cloudflare Pages redirect contract (AR-9 / Story 1.7).
#
# HOW THIS FILE SHIPS: Vite copies everything in `public/` verbatim to `dist/`,
# so this file is served by Cloudflare Pages at `/_redirects` (deployed root).
#
# ORDERING RULES (do not reorder):
#   1. Cloudflare `_redirects` is FIRST-MATCH-WINS — a request tests rules top
#      to bottom and takes the first match.
#   2. STATIC FILES BEAT REDIRECTS — any request whose path matches a real file
#      in `dist/` (e.g. `/assets/<hash>.js`, `/sitemap.xml`, `/robots.txt`,
#      `/images/favicon.png`, `/assets/bg-space.jpg`, `/_redirects` itself) is
#      served as-is and never reaches the rules below.
#   3. HISTORIC 301s come FIRST (preserve previously-indexed inbound links — FR-13).
#   4. The SPA fallback `/* /index.html 200` comes LAST so React Router owns
#      every unmatched path (deep links like `/p/<slug>` resolve, no edge 404).
#      `200` is an INTERNAL REWRITE, not a redirect — the browser keeps the
#      original URL and RR7 renders the route client-side.
#
# SCOPE (Story 1.7 vs Epic 2):
#   Story 1.7 ships the GENERIC historic redirects below + the SPA fallback.
#   The PER-POST `/writing/<slug> → /p/<slug>` 301 map is deferred to Story 2.2
#   (Epic 2) — it needs per-slug fidelity once the 16 essays are migrated.
#   Epic 2 inserts those rules in the marked slot BELOW, BEFORE the catch-all.

# --- Generic historic 301s (retired/renamed routes → new destinations) ---

# Old About page → Landing (About is now the home identity surface, FR-1).
/about    /        301
# Retired Gallery + Reading pages → home.
/reading  /        301
/gallery  /        301
# Old standalone Comics page → the unified Feed, filtered to comics.
/comics   /p?type=comic  301

